# DEVDESK-147 (A-10a) — Explorer tree: activity column for create and delete

Story: `docs/product/activity-indicator/stories.md` §A-10a. UX: `ux.md` §1.2, §5 (legend).
Inventory: `inventory.md` row "Explorer arbre" and gap 3 (validated: create and delete only,
no `WantsBlink`, effort S).
Pattern copied from DEVDESK-144/145/146 (plans `DEVDESK-144-plan.md`, `DEVDESK-145-plan.md`,
commits `a59eef3`, `f475a3b`, `d4d7551`): `datatable.IndicatorColumn` + `SetBlinkPhase`,
`components.RowQuery` / `DescribeRow` / `FailureEvent` / `Status.Detail`, `jobs.Registry`
failures + `ChangedMsg.Failures`, context from `ChangedMsg.Context` (Q1-B of DEVDESK-145, merged),
the activity guard.

Out of scope: the clone list (A-10b, keeps `jobFrame`, `cloneList.setRun(run, frame)` and its
Status frame), the forge index walk (`KindIndex`, global, footer), auth, group children loading
(see Q0).

## Blocking questions (user)

| # | Question | Options | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|
| Q0 | **The brief and `stories.md` disagree** on group children loading. The brief puts "a group loading its children (view-computed state, `WantsBlink`)" in criterion 1. `stories.md` §A-10a criterion 1 says "source: the registry, **without `WantsBlink`**" and lists children loading as out of scope; `inventory.md` gap 3 (validated 2026-11-06) explains why: `TreeNode.Loading` is never drawn on a row — `→` makes the group the current level at once (`navigation.go:26`), so the group is no longer a visible row while its children load; the load is the global footer line `Loading GitLab groups...` (`view.go:139`). The only reachable case is `←` pressed before the answer lands, where the global footer spinner is still on. | **A** follow `stories.md`: registry only (create, delete), no `WantsBlink`, children loading stays the footer spinner · **B** add `WantsBlink()` + a view-computed `Running` for a visible group row with `Loading == true` (only reachable after `←` during a load), plus a footer sentence for it (none is validated in `ux.md` §1.2) | **A**: there is no per-node spinner to remove; B adds a state for a corner case already covered by the footer, and an unvalidated footer phrase. The plan below assumes A. |
| Q1 | **A failed create has no row.** `handleGroupCreated` / `handleProjectCreated` drop the placeholder on failure (`settleCreating(target, nil)`), so criterion 3 ("select the line, the footer gives the cause") cannot hold for a create as the code stands. The remembered failure is keyed on the *predicted* path, and nothing refuses a name that already exists, so that key can be the path of a healthy existing row. | **A** keep a failed placeholder row showing `⊗` until the next create with the same name, `ctrl+r` or a view rebuild; effort M (a node flag the registry does not know, so a rebuilt view loses the row while the registry keeps the failure; dedupe on retry; every action refused on it) · **B** as today, row dropped; read `create` failures on every row → a failure on an existing name paints a healthy row `⊗ last create failed` that no create can clear · **C** as today, row dropped; read the `create` kind only on placeholder rows (`node.Creating`), so a create failure is the 3 s `Error` (`Failed to create g/app — <cause>`) plus the failed run in `:jobs`, and never a `⊗`. Delete failures get the full criterion 3. | **C**: keeps the story at S, never marks a healthy row, and the legend's "stays until the next attempt on that row" stays true. A is a UX change of its own (a row that outlives its request). Criterion 3 is then met for delete and, for create, by the event and `:jobs` only. |
| Q2 | **Same defect outside the explorer.** A create/delete run is admitted with its item `queued` and no message ever moves it to `running` (the work goes out at once, there is no queue). So `:jobs` shows `◴` for a delete in flight and `Run.Stoppable()` returns **true**: `K` is offered and would mark the delete `skipped` while the forge is still deleting. `jobsview` tests only use hand-built `ItemRunning` runs, so they pass. Step 1 fixes it for the explorer (criterion 4). `ws` delete (`workspaces/jobs.go:37`) and `:files` delete (`filebrowser/jobs.go:16`) have the same defect. | **A** fix the explorer here, open a bug for `ws` and `:files` · **B** switch all three to the new constructor in this story (touches two views outside the scope; `ws` "deleting" text and tests change) | **A**: same helper, one-line change each later, reviewed with their own views. |

Hypotheses (prudent default, no question):
- H1 **Kinds per row** (D5): `delete` on every row; `create` only on a placeholder row (`node.Creating`). A real row that shares a path with an in-flight create (existing name) no longer blinks for it — today both rows spin. `KindIndex` and `KindClone` are never read on a tree row.
- H2 **Selection mode** (`ModeSelecting`): the column's rest is the checkbox (as today). Running/queued rows keep their glyph (the toggle refuses them, `selection.go`). A `Failed` row is shown at rest (its checkbox) in selection mode, otherwise the user cannot see whether it is ticked; the footer keeps the selection line, without row detail.
- H3 **Guards unchanged**: `busy()` / `actionable()` / `busyMessage` / `reasonNotCreatedYet` stay as they are (registry-wide, not context-filtered). A failed row is as actionable as an idle one (`D`, `W`, `space`). The explorer offers no `K` (none today); criterion 4 is checked in `:jobs`.
- H4 **Events use the shared builder** (A-05 crit. 8): delete failure `Failed to delete <path> — check logs` (`FailureEvent(KindDelete, msg.Target, msg.Transition().Detail)`) replaces `Delete failed — check logs`; create failure `Failed to create <target> — <cause>` from the transition's `Detail` (the template-unavailable case becomes `Failed to create g/app — template unavailable — nothing was created`, replacing `Could not fetch the template — … Check logs`). The template-commit `Warn` (project exists, empty) is unchanged.
- H5 **No per-frame rebuild**: `handleFrameMsg` sets the blink phase and the footer frame; the tree rows are rebuilt on `ChangedMsg` and on tree changes only. The clone list keeps its per-frame `setRun` (A-10b).
- H6 **Footer frame writers unchanged** (`handleSpinnerTick` during load/refresh, `handleFrameMsg` always): `TestAFrameMovesTheFooterSpinner` keeps passing; not in the criteria.
- H7 **60 columns**: column 0 keeps `IconColumnWidth`; no width threshold moves; `RenderedWidth() == 58`.
- H8 The node type stays readable by name and position during the operation (stories H5).

## Where the state lives — decided by A-04/A-07, not reopened

`jobs.Registry` (router-owned): failure posed by `Apply(failed)`, cleared by `Start` and
`Apply(done)`, forgotten on `delete` done; per context; never on disk. The explorer holds the
copies `ChangedMsg.Runs/Failures` and `ChangedMsg.Context` (Rule 110). Key =
`(kind, FullPath, context)`; a forge path is not absolute, so `jobs.TargetKey` keeps it verbatim.

## Steps (TDD — tests first, each step green and mergeable alone)

Base command for every step:
`go test ./internal/ui/forge/explorer/ ./internal/jobs/ ./internal/ui/jobsview/ ./internal/app/ && go vet ./...`
Step 5 adds `mise run lint`, `go test -count=2 ./internal/app/`, `mise run test-race` (cgo).

### Step 4 — Footer: row detail and failure events (criteria 2, 3) · S (after 2; same files as 3, run after 3)

Files: `view.go` (`status()`), `delete.go` (`handleDeleteComplete`), `create.go`
(`handleGroupCreated`, `handleProjectCreated`), new `footer_test.go`.

```go
